+{"bill":"audit-cycle-anchor-act","seat":"c1a00006","vote":"yes","digest":"1af1f6029604518c6bce8ff67b91f941495db700ee3c70c56ce53b274e3edfaf","reason":"Yes on the narrow legacy-recovery mechanism. It defines audit cycle prospectively, confines the legacy marker to two named pre-anchor trails at 2c6d695, hashes each row at its introducing commit, requires independent re-derivation, keeps rows append-only with no invented cycle identity, and adds seven fail-closed tests. The header's 'no vote authorised' is a stale pre-s8/s9 status; its own stated condition (s8 red-team + s9 response present) is met. Residuals T24 (drafter/sponsor/reviewer overlap), same-substrate review, and marker not compelling a correction are disclosed and contained, not blocking."}
